## (1) exit status 3 is UCRT abort()'s signature, measured

The harness reported `process exit code = 0x3` and the thread's exit code 3 in §38, §40, §42, §44.
Before reading anything into it, measure what the C runtime does on the two ways a process can die:

    ctypes.cdll.msvcrt.abort()   in a child python  → returncode 3
    os.abort()                   in a child python  → returncode 3221226505 (0xC0000409, fastfail)

So status 3 is not "some step of our sequence" and not a Windows OOM or access-violation code: it is
the abort() exit status. `libs/quickjs/quickjs.c` calls plain `abort()` (30 sites), and build.zig:8-14
compiles that file straight into the DLL.

